hey guys it's Jenna here so most of you  probably know that I have been increased  for the past three weeks I had the most  amazing time and I filmed my entire  travel there as well you got to watch  the video it was beautifully shot and  created by a close friend Adam and  myself and I have to say it is probably  one of my best videos so be sure to  click on the link in my description box  watch the video and let me know what you  think so during my long hours of travel  I like to keep myself occupied by  listening to audible there is a huge  selection of health and fitness  audiobooks to choose from and you know  what it is so convenient to access them  straight from my phone so with constant  traveling and having very little time to  read audible has actually allowed me to  keep myself updated with new and  interesting information within the  health and fitness industry I started  listening to the body book by Cameron  Diaz on audible the body book teaches  you how to love your body by first  understanding this amazing vehicle your  body so what I really like about this  book is that it's presented in a really  fun practical and also  easy-to-understand manner you can get  this book for free by going to  audible.com/veritasium box and sign up  to the 30 day free trial so whenever we  travel it is typically difficult to eat  healthy that wasn't the case when I was  in Greece I had the most amazing  Mediterranean diet for three weeks and I  have to say that it has helped me to  stay in shape so I'm sure most of you  have heard about the Mediterranean diet  and why it is also one of the world's  healthiest diet the fundamental of this  diet is really simple and it is  something we have spoken about over and  over again which is to eat real food  focusing on lots of vegetables fruits  whole grains protein and also healthy  fats what I really like about this diet  is that there is no restriction or  needing to go crazy about counting  calories so when I was in Greece I was  really impressed to only find one  McDonald's in the entire city  Center so I asked the locals they told  me that McDonald's tried to conquer  their country back in the 90s but failed  miserably  that's because the Greek people still  prefer their own local freshly cooked  food so I want to share with you my  observations and experience going on the  Mediterranean diet for three weeks and  why it can help you to maintain a  healthy weight long term and also to  lose weight the first observation is Ave  Pal on lots of vegetables and fruits  everybody knows a Greek salad and you  can pretty much see it being served on  every table as a starter having a big  bowl of salad is a great way to study  milk because it is very filling low in  calories and you will end up eating less  for your main course the Greeks do also  eat a lot of vegetables dishes some of  my favorites include briam mix roasted  vegetables stuffed vegetables with rice  I absolutely love this and also dough  mother's stuffed vine leaves which I had  of the opportunity to make so whether  it's raw or cooked vegetables make  vegetables at the center of your meals  the second observation is that fats are  not forbidden when we mention our lives  we tend to think about the Mediterranean  they love the olive oil and they will  literally have it in everything from  their cooking to salad to dipping in  bread and even to include into their  beauty products do you know what I am  really envious on how cheap it is over  there because in Malaysia olive oil is  rather expensive and when it comes to  buying olive oil there are certain tips  which I've learned so you always want to  make sure that it is extra virgin olive  oil the lower the acidity the higher the  quality so go for 0.4% or less and  always buy them in dark bottles heat and  light can damage the oil by creating  oxidation which causes it to lose all  its benefits so here's your challenge  swap your lard butter or margarine with  olive oil it is said that just two  tablespoons of olive oil every day  help with weight loss even though it is  healthy fat it is still very high in  calories so remember to consume in  moderation  the next observation is the Greeks love  to use a lot of herbs and spices to  flavor their food so as I've mentioned  before herbs and spices is the best way  to flavor your food without the extra  calories so if you want to make your  food taste good without the extra  calories swap your heavy cream and also  sources with herbs and spices next the  Greeks consume dairy in moderation Greek  yogurt oh my god it tastes so good  it is so rich creamy full of flavor and  low in calories I just love how the  Greeks use Greek yogurt in everything  from making dips to use as cream topping  on desserts and of course the best is to  make ice cream so you won't find ketchup  chili or barbecue sauce on the table  because who needs them when you have  Greek yogurt to go with everything  here's a really simple comparison 100  gram of full fat Greek yogurt has about  100 calories 100 gram of heavy cream has  345 calories so if you're watching your  waistline but still want to enjoy the  flavor of full fat cream opt for Greek  yogurt instead trust me you will not be  able to tell the difference so when I  was hiking in Madeira with a tour guide  halfway through our hike he took out his  snack box and offered me some nuts seeds  and also dried fruits and I was like  whoa you guys actually snack on this  stuff I thought it's only for the health  freaks so apparently that is their  regular snack and you can in fact see a  lot of vendors selling them by the  street so I challenge you to swap your  sugar salt and fat loaded biscuits  crisps and chocolate bars with nuts  seeds dried fruits and legumes my next  observation is the Greeks enjoy their  seafood fish port  and would limit the red meat intake so  when I was increased I was so happy to  be eating the entire fish to myself and  also lots of seafood so limit red meat  to once a week and enjoy a lot more  fresh fish seafood and also poetry but  remember that at the center of a  Mediterranean diet is still focusing on  lots of vegetables and here's the good  news for other bread pasta and also rice  lovers bread pasta and rice is a huge  part of the Mediterranean diet yep  we are not going for low carb on low  carb whenever you dine in a basket of  freshly baked bread will always be  served I did enjoy it but I have to be  honest after a while it was a little too  much for me  the bread will always fill me up before  my main course came but what I really  enjoyed was the stuffed vegetables with  rice and also dominoes which are  repeated so many times and without even  realizing I was pretty much a vegetarian  for most of my meals so carbon levels of  vegetarians you will not feel deprived  next what your cooking methods the way  you cook your meal can either turn it  into a really healthy meal that is  really good for your body or it can turn  into a high fat greasy meal and make you  feel really crappy so the Greeks rarely  deep-fry their food the meals are  typically baked grilled boiled or  roasted by just changing the way you  prep your meals you will be amazed on  how many calories you can cut down to  the Greeks eating is a daily event so  just ask yourself when was the last time  you set around the table with your  family and friends and enjoyed a really  good meal well to the Mediterranean  people probably every single day so  instead of just gobbling down your  entire meal in front of the TV for the  next week I want you to sit at a table  and give eating the priority it deserves  I can promise you your food would taste  so much better and you will be able to  tune in to your body's hunger and  fullness signal  you will know when you're satisfied when  to stop and avoid overeating and finally  they know how to treat themselves they  love their sweet desserts as well  who loves baklava there is nothing 